sections.explanation:
Loops repeat execution while a condition is true:

```java
// Traditional for loop
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    System.out.println(i);
}

// While loop
while (condition) {
    // runs while true
}

// Do-while loop
do {
    // runs at least once
} while (condition);
```

- `break` exits the loop immediately.
- `continue` skips the remainder of the current iteration.

